                <person xml:id="WAR01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Benjamin Parsons</forename>
                        <surname>Symons</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1785-01-28">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1878-04-12"/>
                    <occupation>warden of Wadham</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Warden of Wadham from 1831 to 1871. Godwin writes to him once, in 1836, along with a Professor
White.  Symons was evangelical and clashed with the 
Tractarians.  He was also opposed to University reform.<lb/>

'He was increasingly at odds 
with his own fellows over the 
admission of dissenters and the opening of
 fellowships to competition.' (<title>DNB</title>)'<lb/></p>
                        <p>There is no letter from 'Warden' or 'Symons' in either the Abinger or the Wadham College records  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>. </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
